# Home: bring the target's arms to the program's start, through the twin (ADR-0071,
# ADR-0072: the target names which sides - the simulation, the real arm, or both).
#
# `cite_bringup.program.cycle.home`, the sequence `./scripts/home` runs:
# initialize every physical arm, measure the start on every side, and only where
# a side is not there move both arms there with one signal; then measure again.
# Nothing is retried. On a pair with a physical side the console first reads the
# twin's mode as SIM and asks the operator to clear the cell (ConfirmOperator),
# and puts the twin back in SIM afterwards. Rejected unless Start robot has
# succeeded and the console is READY. Cancelling the goal is the same software
# stop as StopCell. A success sets ConsoleState.at_start.
#
# Served under the plan's `console.home` (ConsoleState.msg).

float64 speed_scale     # (0, 1] of the program's own speed, sent explicitly by
                        # the operator's panel. Never defaulted: a goal with 0, or
                        # any value outside (0, 1] or below
                        # ConsoleState.minimum_speed_scale, is rejected (ADR-0071
                        # decision 2). The floor applies only to a target that
                        # includes the real arm
uint8 target            # ConsoleState.TARGET_SIM, TARGET_REAL or TARGET_TWIN, sent
                        # explicitly by the operator's panel (ADR-0072). Never
                        # defaulted: 0, an unknown value, or a target not in
                        # ConsoleState.available_targets is rejected
---
bool success
string detail           # what was done, or which step failed and why
---
string step             # the step being done now, as the operator reads it
